      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! I have the answer directly from the wiki.\n\nAccording to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by:\n\n1. **Never holding the key in the Hub\u0027s process environment** \u2014 the Hub does not store the API key in its own environment variables.\n\n2. **Local secrets loader at startup** \u2014 a local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup.\n\n3. **Injection into child processes only** \u2014 the loader injects the key into the environment of spawned child processes (both the Ingest agent and Query agent) immediately before those processes start, rather than into the Hub\u0027s own environment.\n\n4. **Hub\u0027s process remains unmutated** \u2014 the Hub\u0027s process environment is never mutated to contain the key.\n\nThis design means that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the credential simply by inspecting its own environment variables \u2014 the key exists only inside the short-lived child processes that actually need it to call the Anthropic API.",
